INSTALL
=======

You need: a 2006-era SuperSmash.swf (the author archived it on
archive.org, item `supersmashflash_swf`), Node.js >= 18, and a browser
with WebAssembly. That is all. No npm install, no build server.

1. Put SuperSmash.swf next to this file (it is .gitignored on purpose).

2. Get Ruffle (MIT/Apache, upstream https://github.com/ruffle-rs):
   download the `web-selfhosted` zip from a release, unpack into
   ./ruffle/ so you have ruffle.js and the two *_bg.*.wasm files.

3. Build the bundle:

       node tools/build-singlefile.mjs

   Output: ssf1.html, roughly 48 MB, everything embedded. Open it in
   any modern browser, from disk, no server, no network. It works by
   answering Ruffle's wasm fetches from blobs built out of base64
   payloads baked into the page.

4. Or run it the boring way: drop SuperSmash.swf onto any page with
   Ruffle's loader, or into the Ruffle desktop app, or online at
   ruffle.rs demos with local upload.

NOTHING IN STEP 3 LEAVES YOUR MACHINE. The bundle embeds the .swf, and
the .swf embeds third-party characters. Keep the bundle private. This
repo stays legal by not containing it.
